{
  "_comment": "In-house optical mocap BVH (Xsens MVN bone naming) -> Unitree G1. Rotation offsets are calibrated in three steps (see tools/retarget_mocap_g1.py, the CHANGELOG.md entry and the notes below): (1) pelvis/legs from a standing pose that the validated bvh_lafan1_to_g1 offsets reproduce -> approximately [-0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5]; (2) shoulder_yaw_link twist about the upper-arm axis, chosen so shoulder_yaw ~ 0; (3) elbow/wrist offsets propagated down the chain as O_child = mean(R_h_child^-1 R_h_parent) O_parent, which pins the mean elbow flexion to the human's (~5 deg) instead of letting the IK bend the elbow to satisfy an unknown twist. Note the G1's elbow joint zero is an 82 deg bend (joint range [-60, +97.4] deg), so the elbow offset carries an extra +85 deg about the elbow hinge axis (0,1,0). Identity offsets (as in bvh_xsens_to_g1.json) pitch the G1 root 90 deg -- the robot lies on its side -- and also make the IK jitter ~5 cm per frame on the root. The leg/root scale is 0.86 (not 0.90) because the 007bao performer's pelvis sits at 0.947 m vs LAFAN1 ~0.89 m; at 0.90 the G1's feet float ~3 cm.",
